# Independent canonical context manuscript delta review

No blocking finding. Scope is Carson's two manuscript deltas against the complete normative Markdown changes from e45323f to ce0b520850822e199178518f241785ca6c608d53. This is independent review of another author's synchronization, not a new full-content certification of every earlier paragraph. I directly read both source diffs, both complete draft diffs, authoring.md and the existing Gloss-derived Kanji-only Ruby / phrase-level Anno rules. The author's manifest was supplemental and every listed byte/hash was verified; it was not the sole basis of review.

Chapter 16 preserves the old draft byte-for-byte around a single insertion. The inserted page_projection sibling subsection has six new prose paragraphs and four ordered-list paragraphs. The following two old paragraphs remain unchanged and now follow the new subsection, matching the Markdown heading's scope. All ten added paragraph/list bodies, independently extracted from the formal Article structure with Ruby bases, match the normative source after removing source soft line wraps and inline-code delimiters. Domain separator and zero byte, UTF-8, length-prefixed u64 big-endian framing, 32-byte digests, page count, registered ordering, six per-page fields and subsequent source/alias hashes remain in order.

Direct semantic reading confirms fixed registry/source/alias inputs, page-ID namespaces, logical projection routes, all-page success before returned output, no discovery or passive registration, mixed legacy /2 byte and body correspondence, and old-only independent operation behavior. Input identity remains distinct from the distribution digest; whitespace/order/other-page aliases invalidate the new context, generated Markdown is not recursively hashed, and old metadata is not changed. New-directory output, shared check path, no canonical rewrite, no write on semantic failure, possible incomplete directory on OS failure and absent completion manifest are all preserved.

All limits remain exact: 128 pages, 10,000,000 source bytes, 1 MiB aliases, 1 MiB registry, 2 MiB Markdown per page, and optional eight-resource output_limits selected before work. Independent per-page parse/lower is distinguished from the one spent output Budget shared across resolution/rendering/anchor/digest/metadata/copy and legacy regeneration. No retry/reset/increase is introduced. Initial usage and pre-receipt usage are named separately, with receipt serialization/final output charges explicitly excluded from the latter; logical allocation allowance is not advertised as measured physical heap.

Chapter 21 replaces only the two obsolete host-status statements. Its final paragraph matches the source display text; the new link is a real Relative target 16-doc-migration.md with no fragment and display 16章. Existing PageSet input identity, nonrecursive digests, same finite Budget and no new budget after stopping remain intact. Typed API no-I/O, host canonical registry and Markdown set export, existing HTML PageSet backend and unproven overall HTML/Web/publication acceptance are correctly separated. No other prose, code or target is reauthored.

Normal prose uses one Sentence literal per sentence, code/link-bearing sentences use explicit constructors. Ruby bases in changed text contain Kanji rather than digits, Latin words, particles or okurigana. Readings inspected include 一度読/いちどよ + み, 後付/あとづ + け, 書込/かきこ + み, 消費済/しょうひず + み, 前置/ぜんち and 一/ひと + つ. No artificial translation, Anno or parallel was added merely to increase feature counts. All named identifiers and code values remain literal.

Independent structural audit parses both full Articles against current forms and checks the ten new source units and final chapter21 paragraph. This Python audit is not production parse/lower/render validation. Root owns those executions; none is inferred or claimed here. Initial author missing ListItem none and intervening budget-source amendment were fixed before this review and remain honestly described in the author's record. No source/manuscript/proof payload was edited by this review; only this ignored evidence directory was written.
